Given, $\mathrm{p}_{\mathrm{A}}: \mathrm{p}_{\mathrm{B}}=1: 2\begin{array}{ll}\therefore & \mathrm{p}_{\mathrm{B}}=2 \mathrm{p}_{\mathrm{A}} \\ \text{ Similarly } & \frac{\mathrm{n}_{\mathrm{A}}}{\mathrm{n}_{\mathrm{B}}}=\frac{1}{2}\end{array}\therefore \mathrm{x}_{\mathrm{A}}=\frac{1}{1+2}=\frac{1}{3}$ and $\mathrm{x}_{\mathrm{B}}=\frac{2}{1+2}=\frac{2}{3}$
Total pressure, $\mathrm{p}_{\mathrm{T}}=\mathrm{p}_{\mathrm{A}} \mathrm{x}_{\mathrm{A}}+\mathrm{p}_{\mathrm{B}} \mathrm{x}_{\mathrm{B}} \begin{aligned}$&=p_{A} $\times \frac{1}{3}+2 p_{A} \times \frac{2}{3}$\\
&=$\frac{1}{3}$ p_{A}+$\frac{4}{3}$ p_{A} \\
&=$\frac{5}{3}$ p_{A}
\end{aligned}
